the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    *a test result* is a test result.
    *a person* is permitted to board *a flight*.
    *a person* is a person; scenario element.
    *a flight* is a flight; scenario element.
    *a test* is a test; scenario element.
    *a person* has a ticket for *a flight*; scenario element.
    *a person* took a covid test *a test*; scenario element.
    *a flight* is scheduled to depart at *a time*; scenario element.
    the result of *a test* was *a test result*; scenario element.
    *a test* was administered at *a time*; scenario element.

the knowledge base covid_test includes:

the text of the Covid Test Rule is at "sources/covid_test.md".

the text of the Blawx project is at "sources/covid_test.yaml".

% The Act, section by section.
positive is a test result, as stated in the Covid Test Rule at section 1.

negative is a test result, as stated in the Covid Test Rule at section 1.

rule section_1 with provenance the Covid Test Rule at section 1:
a person is permitted to board a flight if
    the person is a person
    and the flight is a flight
    and a test is a test
    and the person has a ticket for the flight
    and the person took a covid test the test
    and the flight is scheduled to depart at a time T
    and the result of the test was negative
    and the test was administered at a time N
    and a number M = T - N
    and M <= 259200.

scenario can_fly is, as stated in the Blawx project at test can_fly:
    % This test is for use in the scenario editor.
    can_fly expects answers [].

scenario good_test is, as stated in the Blawx project at test good_test:
    bob is a person.
    flight_to_hawaii is a flight.
    bobs_test is a test.
    bob has a ticket for flight_to_hawaii.
    bob took a covid test bobs_test.
    the result of bobs_test was negative.
    bobs_test was administered at 946710000.
    flight_to_hawaii is scheduled to depart at 946796400.
    good_test expects answers ["bob is permitted to board flight_to_hawaii"].

scenario old_test is, as stated in the Blawx project at test old_test:
    bob is a person.
    flight_to_hawaii is a flight.
    bobs_test is a test.
    bob has a ticket for flight_to_hawaii.
    bob took a covid test bobs_test.
    the result of bobs_test was negative.
    flight_to_hawaii is scheduled to depart at "datetime(2000,1,5,0,0,0)".
    bobs_test was administered at "datetime(2000,1,1,0,0,0)".
    old_test expects answers [].

query can_fly is:
    which person is permitted to board which flight.

query good_test is:
    bob is permitted to board flight_to_hawaii.

query old_test is:
    bob is permitted to board flight_to_hawaii.

the view the act is:
    the title is "Covid Test Rule, as Blawx encodes it".
    the case is a scenario, with the documents it is stated in.
    the facts about "the case" are
        a person is a person,
        a flight is a flight,
        a test is a test,
        a person has a ticket for a flight,
        a person took a covid test a test,
        a flight is scheduled to depart at a time,
        the result of a test was a test result,
        a test was administered at a time.
    the result is the answer to query can_fly.
    the result shows its reasons.
    the result shows its citations.
    the result can be flipped.

